# cook_app Riverpod

Use Riverpod for shared dependencies and shared business state. Leave ephemeral UI in the widget. Widgets still talk to the view model; the view model talks to repositories.

## Use a provider

- `@Riverpod(keepAlive: true)` only when disposal drops app-wide state or a connection: `tokenStorage` (cached token and `refreshListenable`), `dio` (`client.close`), `GoRouter` (navigation stack). Compose them with `ref.watch`. Release resources in `ref.onDispose`.
- A stateless repository such as `authRepository` stays autoDispose. The screen view model `ref.watch`es it and drops with the page.
- Drive `GoRouter` redirects with `refreshListenable`. Do not `ref.watch` auth state that changes on login; that recreates the router and drops the stack.
- Widgets that read providers: `ConsumerWidget` or `HookConsumerWidget`. `ref.watch` in `build`. `ref.read` in callbacks.

A class with no lifecycle of its own stays a constructor argument. `AuthService` is created inside `authRepository`, not its own provider.

## Do not use a provider

Form fields, `TextEditingController`, `FocusNode`, obscure toggles, and one-screen animation (`GazeBus`, character stage) stay in `flutter_hooks` or `StatefulWidget`.

## Commands

A button submission (login) is a `Mutation` from `package:hooks_riverpod/experimental/mutation.dart`. Do not use `FutureProvider`, or an `AsyncNotifier` whose only state is loading/error, for that.

Put the mutation on the view model as a `static final`, so `ref.watch` sees a stable listenable. The view model constructor takes the repository. Its provider watches both `authRepositoryProvider` and that mutation, and exposes the mutation state on the view model. The widget watches only the view model provider and calls `viewModel.signIn`. Do not read the repository with `tsx.get` when the constructor already holds it. `Mutation.run` rethrows after recording `MutationError`; call `ignore()` when the form renders that state.

## Verify

After adding or changing Riverpod providers, notifiers, or mutations under `apps/cook_app`, run this from `apps/cook_app` and fix every error and warning before finishing:

```bash
dart analyze
```

The Dart MCP analyzer is not a substitute. It does not see missing experimental exports.
